"""SEC-APIKEY-1 (Sprint 1): per-purpose API keys with O(1) lookup.

Adds the ``key_id`` column to ``integration_clients`` and backfills
existing rows. The column is a short, random, public identifier
that the client sends on every request (e.g. ``kid_3f8a9b2c1d0e4f5a``)
so the auth path is O(1) instead of the previous O(n) full-table
scan + HMAC comparison against every active client.

Operational notes
-----------------
* The ``key_id`` is generated by the migration for existing rows
  via ``encode(gen_random_bytes(8), 'hex')`` (Postgres) or
  ``lower(hex(randomblob(8)))`` (SQLite, for tests).
* New clients created via ``POST /admin/integration-clients`` get a
  ``key_id`` assigned at insert time.
* The column is added as ``nullable=True`` so the migration can
  backfill it; once the backfill is done we tighten it to
  ``nullable=False`` in a follow-up migration once all callsites
  are updated to populate it.
* Downgrade: drops the column and its index.
"""
